Let me write a helper in the script: `killPort(4175)` using netstat/taskkill. Simpler: in PowerShell before running, kill the owners.

Let me: (1) kill leftovers now, (2) patch the script's finally to kill by port using `netstat -ano` parse.

Let me implement in the script:
```js
function killListeners(ports) {
  if (process.platform !== "win32") return
  const out = spawnSync("cmd.exe", ["/c", "netstat -ano -p tcp"], { encoding: "utf8" }).stdout || ""
  for (const line of out.split(/\r?\n/)) {
    const m = line.match(/TCP\s+\S+:(\d+)\s+\S+\s+LISTENING\s+(\d+)/)
    if (m && ports.includes(Number(m[1]))) spawnSync("taskkill", ["/PID", m[2], "/T", "/F"])
  }
}
```
